---
chartdown: 0.4
title: Syntax Tour
key: D
tempo: 90
meter: 4/4
feel: Straight
instruments: cello
---

## Basics
> Numbers or letters. Bars are separated by |.
1 | 4 | 5 | 1
D | G | A | D

## Splitting a bar
> Chords share a bar evenly. Use :beats for uneven splits.
1 4 | 6m 5 | 1:3 4:1 | 5:2 4:1 5:1

## Hold, push, stab
> <1> holds a bar. = continues it. A leading ' is a push. A trailing ! is a stab.
<1> | = | 4 '5 | 1! 5!

## Repeats and endings
|: 1 | 4 | 1 | [1] 5 :| x3
[2] 5 4 5 1 |

## Notes for each player
> MD: Everyone reads this line.
> MD drums, bass: Lock in together on the push.
> MD keys: Pad only. Try the View menu to read just your part.
> MD sax, tpt: Horn line on the second pass.
> MD cello: Long notes, declared in the header as a custom instrument.
{p} 1 {drums: in} | 4 | 5 {bass: walk up} | 1

## Dynamics and cues
> Dynamics: pp p mp mf f ff cresc decresc.
{p} 1 | {mf} 4 {watch me} | {cresc} 5 | {ff} 1~

## Key change
> MD: We go up a whole step. Count it in on the last bar.
@key E
1 | 4 | 5 | 1

## Rests and repeats
x | % | 1 x | 5
